AYUDA["en"]="""JMG AUDIOPROCESADOR 5.1 · HELP

HOW TO USE IT
1. Add files with «Select» or «Add», or drag them onto the file list. Files without audio tracks are not added.
2. Click a track (Ctrl+click for several). Each track keeps its own settings. «Apply to all» copies the active track's settings to the other selected tracks.
3. Adjust the tabs and check the result in Visualization.
4. Press PROCESS: the essentials appear and «🔍 See everything» shows each track with its format and effects (it can be copied). Your original files are never modified. «Cancel» stops the process and deletes anything left half-written.

VOLUME
• Master: raises or lowers everything. Below it, the volume of each channel.
• «Set Master»: measures the track and raises the Master up to the target without exceeding the peak limit (automatic anti-clipping). It never lowers the volume: if the track is already loud, it stays at 0 dB.
• «Auto» of «Volume per channel»: measures the loudness of each channel of the selected tracks and moves their sliders to a cinema balance: the center is not touched, the fronts end up about 3 dB below it, the surrounds about 7 dB and the subwoofer about 6 dB (at most ±6 dB; subwoofer ±3 dB). You can then adjust them by hand.
• «Auto» of the advanced EQ: measures the bass, mids and treble of the fronts, surrounds and center and brings them closer together (at most ±3 dB). It stays in the Advanced EQ per group, where you can adjust it. The subwoofer is not touched.
• Normalization: Loudnorm measures the loudness and sets it exactly to the target, without compressing (a limiter takes care of the peaks). «Normalize» measures now and the adjustment is applied when you PROCESS, in a single pass; if you haven't measured before, it is measured while processing. DynAudNorm evens out quiet and loud parts. SpeechNorm evens out the dialogue (it acts only on the center channel, where the voice is).
• Synchronization: framerate conversion (with or without pitch change) and initial delay (-6000 to +6000 ms).
• «🎯 Calculate delay» and «✂ Fix by parts» (in Synchronization): compare the active track with another one in the list, usually the original language, by its music and effects. «Calculate delay» puts the result in the Initial delay. «Fix by parts» is for tracks assembled in parts: each scene gets its delay and it is applied when processing. If you then change the Initial delay or framerate, measure again. If it is already fixed by parts, pressing it again tells you there is no need to measure it again.
• «▶ Check synchronization» (in Synchronization): the movie plays in a video window with sound, with the track as it will come out (delay, framerate and parts), from the point you choose or from each part. This way you check with your own eyes whether the lips match the voice; at the same moment you can also hear the uncorrected track or the reference one. The movie (the file with the picture) must be in the list.
• «Digital smoothing» (0-5): removes the excess treble of many movies and dubs from the 80s and 90s (harsh S sounds and metallic shine) with a filter that cuts the treble, not an equalizer, on all channels except the subwoofer. 0 = no effect. «Auto» measures the treble of the center and chooses the amount.

PRESENCE / EQ
• Presence: brings out the voice (center channel), music/ambience, effects or the subwoofer. Optional limiter ceiling.
• 3-band EQ and advanced EQ per group (front, rear, center) with free frequency.
• Delay per channel: 0 to 100 ms in 5 ms steps (5 ms ≈ 1.7 m).
• Audio cleanup: background noise reduction (1-2 = subtle), click removal and clipping repair (these two are slow). Its «Auto» only sets something if it finds real background noise; on a clean file it leaves it at 0 and tells you it needs no correction.
• «Auto» in Presence, 3-band EQ, Advanced EQ and Audio cleanup: measures the movie and sets the controls. It is a starting point: if you don't like how it turned out, adjust it by hand. If you press it again without touching anything, it removes what it set and goes back to 0. The Presence one leaves the ceiling at «No limit». The «Other normalizations» one picks the one that suits the movie best: SpeechNorm if there is a lot of contrast and the dialogue is quiet, DynAudNorm if there is a lot of contrast, otherwise Loudnorm.
• The «Auto» and «📏 Set Master» buttons measure a sample of the movie with all the other settings of the track already applied (Master, volume per channel, Presence, EQ, Smoothing, range...), except their own: they measure what will really sound. The advanced EQ per group compares the groups with each other: since Smoothing and the 3-band EQ affect all channels equally, its result changes little, and it does not bring back the treble that Smoothing removes. An «Auto» that is set on the active track shows the word in green; if you change what it set by hand, or press «Reset», it goes off.
• Recommended order: first Presence and/or Dynamic range, then the other effects, and always last the Volume per channel: that way each channel's volume is set on the result of everything else and is easier to control finely.

DYNAMICS / BASS
• Bass Management: moves the speakers' low frequencies to the subwoofer (1 = soft, 5 = full). Double Bass: doubles the lows both ways, from the subwoofer to the speakers and from the speakers to the subwoofer. Both clearly raise the subwoofer, protected against clipping. Its «Auto» sets Double Bass (1-3) if the speakers lack deep bass or the subwoofer is weak; if they are balanced, 0. Default cut: 90 Hz.
• Dynamic range: quiet sounds go down and contrast increases.
• Dynamic processing: 1 Lift (raises quiet parts), 2 Impact (loud parts stand out), 3 both. Strength per group. Set the subwoofer to 0 if you use Bass Management or Double Bass.
• «Auto» in Bass Management, Double Bass, Dynamic range and Dynamic processing: the same, according to what it measures (subwoofer level and dynamic range). If the movie is already fine, it leaves 0 and tells you.

VISUALIZATION
• It is generated automatically when you open the tab and updated if you change any setting. Compares BEFORE and AFTER channel by channel.
• Play before or after, Pause/Resume and Stop. Click a channel = hear only that channel (click again = all).
• Wheel = zoom · drag = pan · double-click = x1 · space bar = start and stop. When zoomed, the waveform moves by itself while playing, with the cursor in the center. Segment: the whole file or the first 5, 10 or 30 minutes. If you change the segment while it is generating, the new one starts without waiting; if you go to another tab, it is interrupted and generates by itself when you come back.
• Editor («✎ Edit the file» box): to finish by hand a single-track WAV, W64 or FLAC file, such as the combined track. Drag on a channel to mark that piece (vertically, several channels; then drag its edges to enlarge or shrink it), type the dB (for example -40 to leave it almost silent) and press «Apply». You can also type the times in «From» and «to». Wheel = zoom. To move the waveform when zoomed: drag with the hand on the top ruler or the channel names, use the bottom bar, the ← → arrows (with Shift, faster) or drag with the right button. Right click = clear the selection. With a piece marked, «■ Stop» goes back to the start of the marked piece.
• «▶ Hear the selection» plays only the marked piece and channels, with the changes applied, at any minute. With unsaved changes, the buttons become «Play WITHOUT CHANGES» and «Play WITH CHANGES»: the latter, and clicking on a channel, play with your changes from any point. «↶ Undo» and «↷ Redo» go step by step.
• When minimized, the program stays as an icon next to the clock (the system tray), which shows how the process is going: left click = the window comes back; right click = menu (cancel the process, what to do when done —nothing, exit or shut down the PC—, open the folder when done, exit). In Output it can be turned off, to minimize to the taskbar as usual. Leaving the mouse over a button, box or slider shows a description, which goes away by itself after a few seconds.
• Advanced options («⚙ Options...» next to the bitrate): the most important settings of each format. AC3 and E-AC3: dialogue level, Dolby Surround / EX, headphones, HDCD converter (AC3 only), preferred downmix and treble cut-off; AAC: coding method and treble cut-off; MP3: quality-based VBR and joint stereo; FLAC: compression (the sound is identical). With «Aften Dolby Digital», the same button opens its settings. Whatever is not touched stays automatic; each track keeps its own. AC3 and E-AC3 also have the room type (large or small) with its mixing level; DTS has ADPCM prediction. FFmpeg's DTS is always constant bitrate: 768 or 1536 kbps, the standard ones (with less, players only give noise). AC3 (Aften and FFmpeg): in 5.1, from 224 to 640 kbps; in stereo, from 96 to 640 (default 192). E-AC3: any bitrate, typed by hand, from 192 kbps in 5.1 (in stereo from 64; default 192). Dolby TrueHD comes after the Dolby ones. Each format also has its «Sample rate» (by default, the original's; DTS only 48 kHz, the standard one), and Aften has it in its window. «📀 DVD/BD...» (after «Clear»): the audio of the main movie of a DVD or a Blu-ray (the disc in the drive, a VIDEO_TS / BDMV folder or an .iso image): all its tracks, as they are and losing nothing, to an .mka that goes into the list. It is saved in Music, unless you chose another output folder. Copy-protected discs cannot be read. Use an unprotected or already decrypted copy, if the law of your country allows it. Ripping straight from the disc is slow and unstable: better make an ISO image first and rip from it. Next to it, «💿 Create ISO...» opens Jmg VideoEncoder's Create ISO window (.iso image of a disc or a folder).
• ⚠ The file does not change until you press «💾 Save», and once saved it cannot be undone. That is why «name_retocada» is created (next time that one is updated) and your file stays intact: you will use twice the disk space until you delete the one you do not want. What you did not touch stays identical, with no quality loss. Saving rewrites the whole file: on a movie it takes from a few seconds to a minute.
• Stereo or Multichannel (5.1 / 7.1) output: in multichannel each channel plays through its own speaker (a solo channel, only through its own). Windows must be set to 5.1 or 7.1 (Sound → your output → Configure).
• Playback here is louder than the file, to match other players: it is only for listening and the result does not change. Keep that difference in mind when comparing it with the processed movie.

OUTPUT
• Channels: by default, the same as the input. 5.1, 4.1, 4.0, 3.1, 2.1, 2.0 (Dolby or Simple stereo) or 1.0 (mono). Unused channels are added into the remaining ones.
• 7.1 sources are output as 5.1: the side channels are mixed into the rear ones.
• Stereo source: 2.0 stays stereo; 5.1 performs an Upmix (with «Remove voice» from front and rear). With Upmix only Presence, the volumes and the equalizers are used; the rest (normalizations, Dynamic range, Dynamic processing, Bass Management, Double Bass, Smoothing and Cleanup) is disabled.
• Formats: AC3, EAC3, DTS, AAC, FLAC, WAV, WAV Split (one WAV per channel), RF64, W64 (Sound Forge), TrueHD and Passthrough (copy without converting). MP3 for 2.0 and 1.0. «Aften Dolby Digital» (default) makes the AC3 with Aften, which gives better dynamic range in movies that have a lot; «AC3», with FFmpeg. Its settings, with «⚙ Aften...» like the other formats' ones (by default, block switching and fixed full bandwidth): CBR or VBR, bandwidth, accuracy, filters, dynamic range (DRC and dialogue level) and the bitstream information for the amplifier (Dolby Surround EX, Dolby Headphone, Standard or HDCD A/D converter, preferred downmix and its levels). Not every device reads a VBR AC3.
• «🎬 To VideoEncoder» (at the top, after «Create ISO»): sends the selected files in the list (or all of them) to Jmg VideoEncoder. If it is open, they go to its list; if not, it opens with them. If it is not found, it asks you to look for it once. Then this program closes (both do not stay open at the same time).
• «MKV with video»: copies the video, subtitles, chapters and covers, and adds the processed tracks. «Audio only»: one file per track.
• «DTS core as a separate track» (with «MKV with video»): DTS-HD tracks (Master Audio or High Resolution) carry a regular DTS inside for devices that do not understand HD; ticked, it also comes out as a separate track, not re-encoded, after the originals.
• «🔍 Search» (Output, next to the cover «➕ Add»; with «MKV with video»): looks the movie up on TMDB and sets the poster you choose as the cover. A cover.jpg or folder.jpg next to the file is used by itself if the video has no cover. It needs your own TMDB key, which is free: the first time, the program explains how to get it (account at themoviedb.org → Settings → API). Without a connection, it simply does not search.
• A track without video (for example, the combined one) goes into that MKV if you select it and the video is in the file list, and it goes first. «Remove Original» takes the track out of the MKV; if you also select it, the processed one takes its place. Passthrough copies the track as it is, also in 2.0, and it is not duplicated.
• «❌ Remove Track»: the track disappears from the list and from the MKV. To get it back, remove the file and add it again. If you clear the processed track title, the track comes out with no name.

COMBINE TRACKS (DUBS AND SYNC)
• Combine does not just join channels: it rebuilds the track and gives you a real 5.1. For example, with the dub in 2.0 (or in a fake 5.1) and the original version in real 5.1, the dubbed voices go to the center and the real music and effects to the other channels.
• «🔀 Combine» (at the bottom, next to «Apply to all»): joins channels from several tracks or files into a single track of up to 7.1. Typical example: the music and effects of the original 5.1 English track with the center (and LFE) of the Spanish dubbed track. Each channel has its own Delay, and the result is saved in the destination folder as «name_combinada_5.1».
• From a stereo track (for example, a 2.0 dub), Source also offers «C (extracted voice)», «L without voice» and «R without voice»: the same as the Upmix front channels (with its «Center presence» and «Remove voice F/R»), without having to run the Upmix first.
• «🎯 Calculate delays»: compares the music and effects of the tracks (without the center, which changes with the language) and sets each one's delay, to the millisecond.
• «🔍 Check sync»: with the delays set, measures the offset every few minutes throughout the movie and shows it minute by minute (✓ up to ±4 ms). It tells you whether it is in sync, always off by the same amount, drifting little by little (different speed), with a jump, or out of sync in parts.
• «✂ Fix by parts»: for dubs assembled in parts, which are fine in some scenes and out of sync in others. It measures every 5 s, finds each scene with its delay (if it drifts, it fixes it with a tiny speed change, with no noticeable pitch change) and cuts at the quietest moments. It is applied when combining with the «Apply the fix by parts» box. If you change a delay or a source, calculate it again.
• If a track is 4 % shorter than the other, it is usually 25 fps (PAL) against 23.976 and the program warns you: convert it first in Volume → Synchronization and combine the converted track.
• Tip: try taking the three front channels from the dub and the subwoofer and rears from the original language. It sounds fine and there is much less to fix. After that, everyone can do as they prefer. With a stereo dub and a multichannel original, Combine already proposes it like that when it opens: the center with the voice extracted from the dub, L and R without voice from the dub, and the subwoofer and rears from the original.
• Tip: after combining with the delay by parts, to perfect it even further, run the synchronization again on the combined track, also by parts (Volume → Synchronization, against the original track). It takes longer, but the sync ends up spot on. The same goes for «🎚 Match tone»: a second pass gives excellent results. Of course, not all movies are the same.
• «Remove the original-language echo»: two dynamic range sliders, front and surround (0-10), with the same curve as the Dynamics / Bass tab: quiet sounds go down little by little, without cuts, and loud ones stay as they are. Raise it on the channels that come from the other language: around 8 the echo of its voices almost disappears, but soft ambience also goes down (you can compensate with the volume of those channels). The center and LFE are not touched. Loud voices over music cannot be fully removed.
• «Center voice only»: when the center comes from the dub and the fronts from the original, it keeps only the voices in the center and removes its music and effects (a door slam drops about 14 dB, the voice barely changes), so they do not sound twice. It uses a voice filter (rnnoise) and does not move the sync.
• «🎚 Match tone»: measures the bass, mids and treble of each dubbed channel and matches them to the same channel of the original track (many 80s and 90s dubs are too bright). It is applied with the «Apply the tone matching» box. If the reference track does not have that channel (for example, English surrounds with the fronts of a 2.0 dub), it uses the tone difference between the two tracks on the channels they share.
• «🎛 Auto range»: measures the echo of the voices in the channels that come from another track, comparing them with the center of that same track, and sets the two «Remove the original-language echo» sliders. It is a starting point: you can then correct them. That track must have its own center.
• The default output is 24-bit FLAC: it loses no quality and takes less space than WAV (you can also choose 16 bits or WAV). When it finishes, the window stays open and the settings are saved. When you close it, the combined track opens in Visualization so you can touch it up and listen to it; «🔀 Back to Combine» takes you back, and the sources, delays, parts, tone, range and format come back, so you can change something without measuring again.
• «Reset»: clears the window (sources, delays, tone, parts, range and boxes) and, after asking you, deletes the saved settings of that combined track. The combined file is not touched.
• «Silence voices of the original»: searches the whole movie for voices leaking into fronts and surrounds and lowers them with long fades that start before the voice. It works like «Remove the original-language echo»: two 0-10 sliders, fronts and surrounds, set how much each group drops (0 = nothing, 6 = -60 dB, 10 = -100 dB), and «🎛 Auto silence» measures the echo of those voices and sets them; you can correct them afterwards. It works on channels that come from a track other than the center's and only while the dub is speaking, to respect songs, music and loud hits. It finds echoes with the center of that original track, and voices on a single channel with a voice filter. It takes a few minutes. ⚠ It is not infallible: a loud voice over music can stay, so listen to the result; remove anything that gets through by hand with the Visualization editor.

GOOD TO KNOW
• Dynamic range and Dynamic processing: only one at a time, and normalizations disable them. Presence works with all effects. The program does this automatically.
• ⚠ Limiter ceiling «No limit»: it may clip if you push the effects hard. To be safe, choose -1 dBFS.
• «Reset» clears the open tab («All» = everything). Presets save and load your settings.
• «↶ Undo» and «↷ Redo» (at the bottom, next to «Reset»): undo and redo, one by one, the last 5 actions: setting changes on any track, adding or removing files, deleting tracks, titles... In every tab except Visualization, which has its own. Also with Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y.
• The 3-band EQ and the advanced EQ are not used together: while one has something set, the other is disabled. The same goes for Master and the volume per channel. Digital smoothing does not go with the equalizers or with Audio cleanup either, nor Audio cleanup with the equalizers, Dynamic range or Dynamic processing. The «Auto» buttons switch off what does not go together and the notice tells you what.
• «Open the destination folder when finished» (Output tab): when processing ends, it opens the folder where the files were saved.
• If something goes wrong, check the Edit/Log tab. The log text can be selected with the mouse and copied (Ctrl+C or right-click → Copy / Copy the whole log).
• «When done» can be changed while processing: whatever is set when it finishes applies. It can also put the PC to sleep (with one minute to cancel).
• The «Auto» buttons of Dynamic range and Dynamic processing switch off the other one and the normalizations, because they work one at a time; the notice tells you which. The Presence one switches nothing off.
• When you close the program its temporary files are deleted, also those left by an unexpected exit: Visualization playback can take several GB.
• On startup, once a day, the program checks GitHub for a new version; if there is one, it asks whether you want to open the download page. It does not download or install anything by itself, and without internet nothing happens.
• Every 45 days, when the program opens, a message reminding you that you can support the project is shown for 5 seconds; it closes by itself and, if you click the support link (there or in «About»), it does not come back.
• «⏸ Pause» (next to PROCESS) stops the processing without losing anything and «▶ Resume» carries on where it was.
• Blu-ray: the language of each audio track and subtitle is read from the disc's playlist (the .m2ts files do not carry it).
• While it is working (processing, combining, ripping, extracting, creating an ISO...), the PC does not go to sleep; the screen can still turn off.
• Every slider, including those in Combine, moves with the keyboard arrows: click the slider and press ← → (one step at a time).

